  <h2 id="test-interest">How to test if biotechnology is genuinely your thing before you commit</h2>

  <p>
    Most students pick a 4-year (or 3+2 year) commitment based on a school textbook and a vague feeling. That is backwards for a decision this size.
  </p>

  <p>
    Before you finalise anything, spend a focused stretch of consistent effort actually testing the field — some people need only a few weeks to know, others take a couple of months, and both are completely normal. What matters is that you do at least one of these for real, not just intend to.
  </p>

